Package: hgr
Title: The hidden grammar of reserving
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Robin", "Van Oirbeek", , "robin.vanoirbeek@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
Description: Implements a unified framework for macro-level reserving in non-life insurance,
    based on the insight that classical reserving methods are credibility estimators.
    Includes the Negative Binomial Chain-Ladder (NB-CL) model, Unified Credibility
    Reserving (UCR), Mack's distribution-free model, classical Bühlmann-Straub
    credibility theory, model-agnostic predictive intervals via the
    Dirichlet-Multinomial parametric bootstrap, and the Compound Negative
    Binomial-Gamma (CNBG) amount-triangle model with its information-ceiling
    diagnostics. UCR nests Chain-Ladder, Bornhuetter-Ferguson, and Cape Cod as
    special cases with data-adaptive credibility weights. The multinomial
    bootstrap provides predictive intervals for any reserving method producing
    development proportions, governed by a single Dirichlet concentration
    parameter c that doubles as a diagnostic for model adequacy. The CNBG model
    characterises what a paid-loss triangle can and cannot identify about
    reserve uncertainty, with a kappa posterior diagnostic that flags when
    amount-only inference is unsupported. Provides functions for model fitting,
    prediction, variance estimation, parametric bootstrap, diagnostics, and
    model comparison.
